Use `TextPainter` with the same width, style, direction, locale, and text scaler that the real `Text` will get, and read `didExceedMaxLines`. Wrap it in a `LayoutBuilder` so you measure against the actual available width.

## Measurement helper

```dart
bool exceedsMaxLines({
  required BuildContext context,
  required String text,
  required TextStyle style,
  required double maxWidth,
  int maxLines = 3,
}) {
  final painter = TextPainter(
    text: TextSpan(text: text, style: style),
    maxLines: maxLines,
    textDirection: Directionality.of(context),
    locale: Localizations.maybeLocaleOf(context),
    textScaler: MediaQuery.textScalerOf(context),
  )..layout(maxWidth: maxWidth);

  final exceeded = painter.didExceedMaxLines;
  painter.dispose(); // avoid leaking the underlying paragraph
  return exceeded;
}
```

## Using it in the widget

```dart
class ExpandableComment extends StatefulWidget {
  const ExpandableComment({super.key, required this.text});
  final String text;

  @override
  State<ExpandableComment> createState() => _ExpandableCommentState();
}

class _ExpandableCommentState extends State<ExpandableComment> {
  bool _expanded = false;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final style = DefaultTextStyle.of(context).style; // match what Text renders
    return LayoutBuilder(
      builder: (context, constraints) {
        final overflows = exceedsMaxLines(
          context: context,
          text: widget.text,
          style: style,
          maxWidth: constraints.maxWidth,
        );
        return Column(
          crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,
          children: [
            Text(
              widget.text,
              style: style,
              maxLines: _expanded ? null : 3,
              overflow: _expanded ? TextOverflow.visible : TextOverflow.ellipsis,
            ),
            if (overflows)
              TextButton(
                onPressed: () => setState(() => _expanded = !_expanded),
                child: Text(_expanded ? 'Show less' : 'Show more'),
              ),
          ],
        );
      },
    );
  }
}
```

Note that the overflow check always runs with `maxLines: 3`, independent of `_expanded`, so the "Show less" button stays visible after expanding.

## Why these inputs matter

- **`maxWidth` from `LayoutBuilder`:** the result is only valid for the width the text will actually render at. Don't use screen width.
- **`textScaler`:** at 150-200% system font size, copy that fit in 3 lines at 1.0 will overflow. Omitting it gives wrong answers for exactly the users who most need the button.
- **`locale` and `textDirection`:** they affect line breaking and shaping, so they matter for localized and RTL copy.
- **Same `TextStyle`:** if you pass a different font size, weight, or height than the rendered `Text`, the measurement drifts. Resolve the style the same way the `Text` does (merge with `DefaultTextStyle`, or use the exact theme style for both).
- **Inline spans:** if the comment uses `Text.rich` (mentions, links), pass the same `TextSpan` tree to the painter rather than a plain string, and keep `WidgetSpan` sizing in mind (use `placeholderDimensions` on the painter if you have them).

## Practical notes

- Measuring in `build` is fine for short comment lists, but in long `ListView`s consider caching the result keyed on `(text, maxWidth, textScaler, locale)` to avoid re-laying out on every rebuild.
- Don't apply the non-breaking-space orphan trick here for non-space-delimited languages (CJK, Thai). It would change line breaks and make your measurement disagree with the real text unless you measure the same transformed string.
- Test long unbroken strings (URLs, long German compounds) too. They can overflow in fewer "words" than you expect.

## Test it

```dart
testWidgets('shows "Show more" only when copy exceeds 3 lines at 2x scale', (tester) async {
  Future<void> pump(String text) => tester.pumpWidget(
        MaterialApp(
          builder: (context, child) => MediaQuery(
            data: MediaQuery.of(context)
                .copyWith(textScaler: const TextScaler.linear(2.0)),
            child: child!,
          ),
          home: Scaffold(
            body: SizedBox(width: 200, child: ExpandableComment(text: text)),
          ),
        ),
      );

  await pump('Hi');
  expect(find.text('Show more'), findsNothing);

  await pump('A much longer localized comment ' * 10);
  expect(find.text('Show more'), findsOneWidget);
  expect(tester.takeException(), isNull);
});
```

Also run it at `TextScaler.linear(1.0)` and `1.5`, with a short, realistic, and long localized string, and in a narrow card width.
